  <ym-title|Harvested owner energy at rank threshold \V draft
  evidence><label|harvested-owner-energy-at-rank-threshold--draft-evidence>

  Parent-authored under issue #26, session hairer-codex-existence-20261111,
  claim until 2026-11-12 16:40 UTC. Source pin
  <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>. Text:
  <verbatim|manuscript/existence/actual-harvested-owner-energy.tex>.
  Unintegrated, independent review requested. No full-proof closure claim.

  <section|Exact route><label|exact-route>

  All paths in the first group begin <verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/>.

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|Pockets.lean>, namespace
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Wax>: <verbatim|fineCharge>,
    <verbatim|flickers>; private <verbatim|listed>, <verbatim|relief>,
    <verbatim|pocket_price>, <verbatim|tilted_cost>. Target t remains in
    [nu/2,2nu], seed inventory unchanged. Listed chord lower bound becomes
    t/8, guide smallness sqrt(a)/16, and direct small-seed constant a/512.
    Path-discard count stays on fine lattice; LaneCounts are re-established
    at changed t, not transported by continuity. Targeted reads include
    listed, relief statement, the whole pocket_price tail and
    tilted_cost/flickers.

    <item><verbatim|Attic.lean>, same Wax namespace: <verbatim|reserve_lane>,
    <verbatim|stakeBook>, <verbatim|RankMeter>, <verbatim|chamber>; private
    <verbatim|selections>, <verbatim|icehouse>, <verbatim|ice>,
    <verbatim|boost>. Full read. The new subsection writes the inventory
    comparison V\<less\>=R+2nu<em|n0, nu>#N\<less\>=2R, T*#K\<less\>=V and
    its exact allocation conditions. The unchanged E05/E07/E08/E09 rows are
    reused from seed-energy/hit/unhit chapters. Chosen m is bounded by
    penalty/32, coarse direct/64, fine linear/32, (fine direct/512)/32. After
    L, width W and then entrance x are chosen.

    <item><verbatim|Reheat.lean>, namespace
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank>: <verbatim|crossfade>, plus
    <verbatim|retime>, <verbatim|burst_limit>, <verbatim|tall_limit> already
    inspected. Fine tau=phase(betaF x), nu=fiery(retime x); compare within
    factor two, not equate. <verbatim|crossfade> and preceding tone_ratio
    proof tail reread.

    <item><verbatim|Hearth.lean>, Wax namespace: <verbatim|reread>,
    <verbatim|depth>, <verbatim|Peaking>, <verbatim|spun>,
    <verbatim|preheat>; private <verbatim|rim>. Full read. Exact threshold
    replacement on clean annular rows follows from two explicit kept tests;
    no continuity claim. Annulus error \<less\>=b/2<em|nu\<twosuperior\> and
    tau\<twosuperior\>\<less\>=4nu\<twosuperior\> give
    b/8>tau\<twosuperior\>. Selected-window chart representation/written
    receipt retained for the actual array.

    <item><verbatim|Opacity/Hulls.lean>, namespace
    <strong|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Milk>>:
    <verbatim|ceilingE>, <verbatim|levy_equ>, <verbatim|reinterpret>,
    <verbatim|Hefts>, <verbatim|launched>. Full read. Important correction to
    earlier audit: these are not in Pump. Packet separation R\<gtr\>=205B,
    annulus radius 200B, span\<less\>=B/50. Signed average uses Aff.weight
    once. Actual subtraction equals harvested extraction; mean columns have
    nonnegative sign and can be dropped. Source threshold is phase(betaF x)
    in the exact launched conclusion.
  </itemize-minus>

  Second group begins <verbatim|Lean/YM/AnalyticBridge/ANNULUS_GAUSSIAN_INTERFACE_1AD/>:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|Payment.lean>, <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.Annulus1AD.Seen>,
    <verbatim|started>. Full read including payment for context. Seen gives
    one clean chart constant K\<gtr\>=1, K\<less\>=width, uniformly for every
    actual SliceSet/Wide annular test. It is not a Fourier annulus statement.

    <item><verbatim|Anchors.lean>, same namespace: <verbatim|harvesting>,
    <verbatim|band_bill> and the tail of <verbatim|band_bought>, plus
    <verbatim|curb_outside>. Targeted reads. Selected Gaussian rows avoid the
    core, and packet separation buys the annular window.

    <item><verbatim|Read.lean>, same namespace: <verbatim|preview> in full.
    Actual signedArray: tree zero, frozen cutoff agrees with the clean chart,
    active doors give bound 2<em|width>fiery. Only exact local clean patches
    are used for frozen logarithms; no global logarithm assumed.

    <item><verbatim|Jets.lean>, same namespace: <verbatim|extracting>, plus
    preceding nonnegative columns proof tail. Exact columns=harvest.extract
    needs actual path Bounds and Authorized branch, supplied by the same
    funded/boosted tube.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Canonical inputs and limitations><label|canonical-inputs-and-limitations>

  Reuse <verbatim|seed-energy.tex>, <verbatim|seed-hit-comparison.tex>,
  <verbatim|seed-unhit-comparison.tex>, <verbatim|seed-tree-patch.tex> and
  <verbatim|packet-annulus.tex>. The latter's actual protected annulus and
  affine row proof is the relevant annulus here, not the distinct Fourier
  response annulus in annulus-same-data-binding.tex. All numerical seed,
  guide, range, chart and branch inputs remain those of these canonical
  proofs and the funded tube; global selected-history purchases must still
  bind them. This section supplies the threshold-change, harvested-array and
  energy-ceiling join, not the independent all-Matched Pupil/socket estimate.

  No new literature result: the changed-threshold inequalities and finite
  reindexing are proved explicitly, and the substantive canonical seed and
  annulus arguments are reused. No Lean edits/build/axiom replay. No TeX
  build yet. Review should check that the original Plot/Wide/Seeded
  hypotheses and all relevant radius requirements really match these
  applications.

